# D4 stage 1 — the real page in the editor + scroll-effect presets: BUILD CONTRACT v1

Owner decision D4 = "Option 1: upgrade the existing storefront editor". This stage delivers (5) the live storefront page in the middle of Admin → Storefront (live as the draft changes, click-to-select synced with Layers + inspector, hover outlines, phone/tablet/desktop, pop-ups in their real display) and (6) scroll-effect presets on any block (gallery, strength, preview slider). Three streams build in parallel: **S** (storefront), **A** (admin), **M** (mobile + backend). Section 11 is the binding, disjoint file-ownership table. Everything named here is normative unless marked SHOULD.

---

## 0. Decisions (read first)

1. **One content system, one renderer.** The centre pane becomes an `<iframe>` of a NEW storefront route **`/editor-frame`**. The admin posts the operator's *unsaved* working copy into it with `postMessage`; the frame asks its OWN server to render that JSON through the exact live renderer (`ManagedPage` → `SiteLayoutView` → `PageRenderer` → `SECTION_RENDERERS`, `BrandShell`, `PopupFrame`) by calling a **Next.js Server Action that returns React (RSC) elements**. Reason: `PageRenderer` and most sections are async server components with live data; a client re-implementation would be a second renderer. No new block renderer, no second schema, no publish-on-save, no change to draft → submit → CEO approve.
2. **Drafts never travel any other way.** The frame never fetches a draft (no preview token, no staff-authenticated call). It renders only (a) the JSON the editor posts and (b) public data the live page already reads (live layouts of the surrounding chrome, `/storefront/concepts`, menus, reviews, locations). Nothing is stored server-side; nothing is counted (no `SiteLayoutStat`).
3. **Selection is drawn inside the frame.** In the frame only, every block of the edited layout is wrapped in a `display:contents` marker carrying `data-sv-block="<id>"`. The frame draws hover/selected outlines itself and tells the admin the id plus a rect (rect = hook for stage-7 drag/resize). Live pages never carry these markers.
4. **Scroll effects = `block.motion = { preset, intensity }`** on every block, separate from and composable with the one-shot entrance `animation` (which is untouched). Web: CSS scroll-driven animations (`view-timeline` + `animation-timeline` + `animation-range`) under `@supports`; otherwise a ~2 KB IntersectionObserver/rAF engine drives the SAME `@keyframes` (paused CSS animation, `currentTime` = progress). Reduced motion, missing support without JS, or an unknown preset → no effect, content fully visible. Mobile maps motion to the existing entrance animation.
5. **Layers = the existing row list** (`Canvas.tsx`) moved into a compact left pane; the palette becomes its "Add" tab; the inspector stays right and gains "Scroll effect". `tree.ts` keeps all structure ops. Note: `tree.ts` has NO undo today; undo is stage 7 — do not add a partial one now.
6. **No new API route, no Prisma change, no new npm dependency.** Backend work = zod for `motion` + tests.

---

## 1. Motion schema (4 copies, identical lists)

Copies that must stay in step: `frontend/storefront/src/lib/blocks.ts` (S), `frontend/admin/src/lib/blocks.ts` (A), `mobile/src/content/types.ts` (M), `backend/src/modules/siteLayouts/schemas.ts` (M).

```ts
// Scroll effects (D4 stage 1). Same order and spelling in all four copies.
export const MOTION_PRESETS = ['parallax', 'fade', 'grow', 'pin-reveal', 'sticky-stack', 'side-pan', 'text-reveal'] as const
export type MotionPreset = (typeof MOTION_PRESETS)[number]
export const MOTION_INTENSITIES = ['subtle', 'medium', 'strong'] as const
export type MotionIntensity = (typeof MOTION_INTENSITIES)[number]

/** A block's scroll effect. Absent = none. intensity absent = 'medium'.
 *  Renderers treat an unknown/invalid value as "none" — never hidden content. */
export interface BlockMotion {
  preset: MotionPreset
  intensity?: MotionIntensity
}
// on BaseBlock / BlockBase (storefront, admin, mobile):
//   motion?: BlockMotion   // scroll effect; independent of `animation` (entrance, plays once)
```

Backend zod (M), added to `blockBase` (so it covers top-level blocks, `columns` children via `leafBlockSchema`, and `settings.ab.blocks` via `blocksSchema`):

```ts
export const MOTION_PRESETS = [...] as const      // as above
export const MOTION_INTENSITIES = [...] as const
export const motionSchema = z.object({
  preset:    z.enum(MOTION_PRESETS),
  intensity: z.enum(MOTION_INTENSITIES).optional(),
}).strict()
// inside blockBase:
motion: z.preprocess((v) => (v === null ? undefined : v), motionSchema.optional()),
```
- `null` is accepted and stripped (parsed value undefined → dropped from stored JSON). Unknown preset/intensity, extra keys, non-objects → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` (existing error handler). Old layouts (no `motion`) parse exactly as before; `animation`, `animationDelayMs`, `animationDurationMs` rules unchanged; `MAX_TOP_LEVEL_BLOCKS` / `MAX_CONTENT_BYTES` unchanged.
- Storefront normalisation (S, `lib/motion.ts`): `normalizeMotion(v: unknown): { preset: MotionPreset; intensity: MotionIntensity } | null` — null unless `v` is a plain object whose `preset` is in `MOTION_PRESETS`; intensity outside the list → `'medium'`. The frame renders posted (unvalidated) JSON, so the renderer MUST go through this.
- Where it applies: any block type, incl. `section`, `columns` and column children. Ignored (no effect) by `PopupBlocks` (web pop-ups) — pop-ups do not scroll. The admin offers the control only for layout kinds `page` and `footer` (not `header`, `widget`, `popup`).
- Reserved for later stages (do NOT implement now, do not use these key names for anything else): `keyframes`, `devices`, `range`, `delayMs`. Adding them later is a coordinated 4-copy change.
- Defaults: no motion on new blocks; `cloneBlock`/"Copy A to B" copy it as data (already generic).

---

## 2. The seven presets (exact behaviour)

### 2.1 Table (single source: `frontend/storefront/src/lib/motion.ts` → `MOTION_SPECS`)

| preset | UI name | effect | structure | @keyframes | animation-range (subtle / medium / strong) | inline vars (subtle / medium / strong) | editor scrub | mobile entrance |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `parallax` | Parallax | content drifts up slower than the page | plain | `sv-m-parallax` | `cover 0% cover 100%` (all) | `--sv-m-y`: 24px / 56px / 112px | in place | `fade-in` |
| `fade` | Fade as you scroll | fades in as it scrolls in (and back out scrolling up) | plain | `sv-m-fade` | `entry 0% entry 60%` / `entry 0% entry 100%` / `entry 0% cover 50%` | `--sv-m-o0`: 0.45 / 0.15 / 0 | in place | `fade-in` |
| `grow` | Grow as you scroll | starts smaller, grows to full size | plain | `sv-m-grow` | `entry 0% cover 45%` (all) | `--sv-m-s0`: 0.94 / 0.86 / 0.72 | in place | `zoom-in` |
| `pin-reveal` | Pin and reveal | holds at the top while it opens from a rounded inset card to full size | pin | `sv-m-reveal` | `exit-crossing 0% exit-crossing 40vh` / `… 70vh` / `… 110vh` | `--sv-m-track`: 40vh/70vh/110vh; `--sv-m-inset`: `5% 3%` / `10% 7%` / `18% 12%`; `--sv-m-radius`: 16px / 28px / 40px | in place | `fade-up` |
| `sticky-stack` | Sticky stack | consecutive stack blocks stick at the top; each next one slides over like cards | stack | none | none | `--sv-stack-step`: 8px / 16px / 28px | scroll | `fade-up` |
| `side-pan` | Sideways pan | slides sideways (right → left) as you scroll down | plain | `sv-m-pan` | `cover 0% cover 100%` (all) | `--sv-m-x`: 6vw / 14vw / 26vw | in place | `slide-left` |
| `text-reveal` | Text reveal | fills in top → bottom (faint → full) as you scroll | plain | `sv-m-text` | `cover 10% cover 50%` (all) | `--sv-m-floor`: 0.45 / 0.2 / 0.06 | in place | `fade-up` |

Every preset's NON-animated state is the natural, fully visible element (no transform, opacity 1, no clip, mask at the fully-opaque position). So whenever the animation is not applied (reduced motion, unknown preset, no support + no JS) the content looks exactly like a block without motion (pin/stack keep only their positioning, which reduced motion also removes).

```ts
// lib/motion.ts (S) — shapes; values exactly as the table
export type RangeName = 'cover' | 'entry' | 'exit' | 'contain' | 'entry-crossing' | 'exit-crossing'
export type RangeEdge = { name: RangeName; pct: number } | { name: RangeName; vh: number }
export interface MotionSpec {
  keyframes: string | null                       // @keyframes name in motion.css; null = no animation
  structure: 'plain' | 'pin' | 'stack'
  scrub: 'in-place' | 'scroll'
  range: Record<MotionIntensity, [RangeEdge, RangeEdge]> | null
  vars: Record<MotionIntensity, Record<string, string>>
}
export const MOTION_SPECS: Record<MotionPreset, MotionSpec>
export function normalizeMotion(v: unknown): { preset: MotionPreset; intensity: MotionIntensity } | null
export function rangeCss(r: [RangeEdge, RangeEdge]): string        // 'entry 0% cover 50%', 'exit-crossing 0% exit-crossing 70vh'
export function motionVars(m): Record<string, string>   // spec vars + '--sv-m-name' (if keyframes) + '--sv-m-range' (if range)
export function rangeProgress(r, top: number, H: number, V: number): number   // JS mirror, §2.4
export function hasMotion(blocks: unknown): boolean     // any valid motion, top level or inside columns
```
`lib/motion.ts` must be isomorphic (no `'use client'`, no server-only imports): used by the server wrapper, the client fallback engine and the frame.

### 2.2 DOM structures (rendered by S's `MotionWrap`, server component, `components/blocks/Motion.tsx`)

`motionVars` are set as inline custom properties on the wrapper. No wrapper gets `position: relative` or any other layout style.

```html
<!-- plain: parallax, fade, grow, side-pan, text-reveal -->
<div class="sv-motion" data-sv-motion="fade" data-sv-intensity="medium"
     style="--sv-m-name: sv-m-fade; --sv-m-range: entry 0% entry 100%; --sv-m-o0: 0.15">
  <div class="sv-motion-target"> …existing block output… </div>
</div>

<!-- pin: pin-reveal -->
<div class="sv-motion" data-sv-motion="pin-reveal" data-sv-intensity="medium"
     style="--sv-m-name: sv-m-reveal; --sv-m-range: exit-crossing 0% exit-crossing 70vh; --sv-m-track: 70vh; --sv-m-inset: 10% 7%; --sv-m-radius: 28px">
  <div class="sv-motion-pin"><div class="sv-motion-target"> …block… </div></div>
  <div class="sv-motion-track" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</div>

<!-- stack: sticky-stack (consecutive siblings grouped by PageRenderer, §3.2) -->
<div class="sv-stack" style="--sv-page-bg: <brandSurface(concept).bg when the page is a brand page>">
  <div class="sv-motion sv-stack-card" data-sv-motion="sticky-stack" data-sv-intensity="medium" data-sv-stack-first="" style="--sv-stack-i: 0; --sv-stack-step: 16px"> …block… </div>
  <div class="sv-motion sv-stack-card" data-sv-motion="sticky-stack" data-sv-intensity="strong" style="--sv-stack-i: 1; --sv-stack-step: 28px"> …block… </div>
</div>
```
The view-timeline subject is always the untransformed `.sv-motion` wrapper; the animated element is `.sv-motion-target` (pin: the target inside the sticky `.sv-motion-pin`). The pin wrapper's height = block + track, so the sticky child has room to stay pinned; the track height is static CSS → no layout shift.

### 2.3 `frontend/storefront/src/components/blocks/motion.css` (S; imported by `Motion.tsx`; NOT in globals.css)

```css
/* Scroll effects for blocks (block.motion). See lib/motion.ts for the values. */
:root { --sv-page-bg: var(--servd-bg); --sv-sticky-top: 0px; }
html:has(.sv-nav) { --sv-sticky-top: 52px; }          /* pins land under the servd glass nav */

.sv-motion-track { height: var(--sv-m-track, 0px); pointer-events: none; }
.sv-motion[data-sv-motion='pin-reveal'] > .sv-motion-pin { position: sticky; top: var(--sv-sticky-top, 0px); }

/* text reveal: the mask is static; only its position animates. black = mask alpha, never painted. */
.sv-motion[data-sv-motion='text-reveal'] > .sv-motion-target {
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black 40%, rgb(0 0 0 / var(--sv-m-floor, 0.2)) 60%);
          mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black 40%, rgb(0 0 0 / var(--sv-m-floor, 0.2)) 60%);
  -webkit-mask-size: 100% 250%; mask-size: 100% 250%;
  -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat; mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  -webkit-mask-position: 0 0; mask-position: 0 0;       /* 0 0 = fully visible */
}

.sv-stack .sv-stack-card {
  position: sticky;
  top: calc(var(--sv-sticky-top, 0px) + var(--sv-stack-i, 0) * var(--sv-stack-step, 16px));
  background-color: var(--sv-page-bg);
}
.sv-stack .sv-stack-card:not([data-sv-stack-first]) {
  box-shadow: 0 -12px 28px -20px color-mix(in srgb, var(--servd-ink) 55%, transparent);
}

@keyframes sv-m-parallax { from { transform: translate3d(0, var(--sv-m-y, 56px), 0); } to { transform: translate3d(0, calc(var(--sv-m-y, 56px) * -1), 0); } }
@keyframes sv-m-fade     { from { opacity: var(--sv-m-o0, 0.15); } to { opacity: 1; } }
@keyframes sv-m-grow     { from { transform: scale(var(--sv-m-s0, 0.86)); } to { transform: none; } }
@keyframes sv-m-reveal   { from { clip-path: inset(var(--sv-m-inset, 10% 7%) round var(--sv-m-radius, 28px)); } to { clip-path: inset(0 round 0); } }
@keyframes sv-m-pan      { from { transform: translate3d(var(--sv-m-x, 14vw), 0, 0); } to { transform: translate3d(calc(var(--sv-m-x, 14vw) * -1), 0, 0); } }
@keyframes sv-m-text     { from { -webkit-mask-position: 0 100%; mask-position: 0 100%; } to { -webkit-mask-position: 0 0; mask-position: 0 0; } }

/* Browsers with scroll-driven animations: pure CSS, works without JS. Longhands only
   (the `animation` shorthand would reset animation-timeline/range). */
@supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
  .sv-motion { view-timeline: --svm block; view-timeline-inset: 0; }
  .sv-motion > .sv-motion-target,
  .sv-motion > .sv-motion-pin > .sv-motion-target {
    animation-name: var(--sv-m-name);
    animation-duration: auto;
    animation-timing-function: linear;
    animation-fill-mode: both;
    animation-timeline: --svm;
    animation-range: var(--sv-m-range);
  }
}
/* Everyone else: nothing until the JS engine marks the wrapper ready, then it scrubs currentTime. */
@supports not (animation-timeline: view()) {
  .sv-motion[data-sv-motion-ready] > .sv-motion-target,
  .sv-motion[data-sv-motion-ready] > .sv-motion-pin > .sv-motion-target {
    animation-name: var(--sv-m-name);
    animation-duration: 1000ms;
    animation-timing-function: linear;
    animation-fill-mode: both;
    animation-play-state: paused;
  }
}
/* Editor preview slider (set only inside /editor-frame), any browser. */
.sv-motion[data-sv-m-scrub] > .sv-motion-target,
.sv-motion[data-sv-m-scrub] > .sv-motion-pin > .sv-motion-target {
  animation-name: var(--sv-m-name) !important;
  animation-duration: 1000ms !important;
  animation-delay: 0s !important;
  animation-timing-function: linear !important;
  animation-fill-mode: both !important;
  animation-play-state: paused !important;
  animation-timeline: auto !important;
  animation-range: normal !important;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .sv-motion:not([data-sv-m-scrub]) > .sv-motion-target,
  .sv-motion:not([data-sv-m-scrub]) > .sv-motion-pin > .sv-motion-target {
    animation: none !important; transform: none !important; opacity: 1 !important; clip-path: none !important;
    -webkit-mask-image: none !important; mask-image: none !important;
  }
  .sv-motion > .sv-motion-pin { position: static !important; }
  .sv-motion-track { display: none !important; }
  .sv-stack .sv-stack-card { position: relative !important; top: auto !important; box-shadow: none !important; }
}
```
S may reformat; semantics must not change. Child combinators (`>`) are required so an outer wrapper never styles an inner block's target (nested motion inside `columns`); nested named timelines resolve to the nearest `--svm` declaration.

### 2.4 Range math (JS mirror of the CSS named ranges; used by the fallback engine)

Subject = the `.sv-motion` wrapper. `top` = `getBoundingClientRect().top`, `H` = its height, `V` = `window.innerHeight`, `s = V - top` (distance travelled since the subject's top reached the viewport bottom). Named range spans in `s`:
- `cover` [0, V+H]; `entry` [0, min(H,V)]; `exit` [max(H,V), V+H]; `contain` [min(H,V), max(H,V)]; `entry-crossing` [0, H]; `exit-crossing` [V, V+H].
- An edge `{name, pct}` = start + pct/100·(end − start). An edge `{name, vh}` = start + vh/100·V.
- progress = clamp((s − s0)/(s1 − s0), 0, 1); if s1 ≤ s0 → s ≥ s1 ? 1 : 0.

### 2.5 Runtime (S)

- `components/blocks/motionClient.ts` (client util, no React): `supportsScrollTimeline()` (= `CSS.supports('animation-timeline: view()')`), `startMotionEngine()/stopMotionEngine()` (ref-counted singleton), `setScrubProgress(wrapper, p): boolean`, `clearScrub(wrapper)`, `scrollStackTo(wrapper, p)`.
- `components/blocks/MotionRuntime.tsx` (`'use client'`, renders nothing): mounted by `SiteLayoutView` when `hasMotion(resolved blocks)`; calls `startMotionEngine()` on mount, stop on unmount.
- Engine (only when `!supportsScrollTimeline()` and NOT `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; listens to the media query's `change` and stops/starts): finds `.sv-motion[data-sv-motion]` whose spec has keyframes (skips `sticky-stack` and any wrapper with `data-sv-m-scrub`), tracks the active set with an IntersectionObserver (`rootMargin: '50% 0px'`), recomputes on passive `scroll`/`resize` via one rAF, rescans on DOM changes (MutationObserver on `document.body`, childList+subtree, rAF-debounced). For each wrapper: set `data-sv-motion-ready` (if absent), then in the SAME frame `const a = target.getAnimations().find((x) => (x as CSSAnimation).animationName?.startsWith('sv-m-'))` and `a.currentTime = progress * 1000`. Before the attribute is set nothing animates, so no-JS shows full content.
- Scrub (editor only, §4.5): `setScrubProgress` sets `data-sv-m-scrub` on the wrapper, then sets `currentTime = p*1000` on the target's `sv-m-*` animation (call `getAnimations()` after setting the attribute). `clearScrub` removes the attribute (scroll-driven state resumes). `scrollStackTo(wrapper, p)` (sticky-stack only): `g = wrapper.closest('.sv-stack')`; `start = g.top(doc) − parseFloat(getComputedStyle(wrapper).top)`; `end = start + max(0, g.height − firstCard.height)`; `window.scrollTo({ top: start + p·(end − start), behavior: 'instant' })`.

### 2.6 Layout / CLS / caveats (documented, not bugs)
- Transforms/opacity/clip/mask cause no layout shift. The pin track is static CSS (SSR) → no shift. Reduced motion removes pin, track and stacking.
- Wrappers sit at block level, outside sections. Page-level ancestors in live routes and the frame use `overflow-x: clip` (body, `.sv-home`), which does not create a scroll container, so view timelines and sticky work. S must not add `overflow: hidden/auto` to any page-level wrapper it creates (frame, PageSurface, stack group).
- Parallax/side-pan move the whole block: on a full-bleed coloured band, Strong can show page background at the band's edges (UI hint). A transform on `.sv-motion-target` becomes the containing block for `position: fixed`/`absolute` descendants inside that block — the admin hides motion for widgets (the fixed feedback button) for this reason.
- sticky-stack needs ≥ 2 consecutive stack blocks (a lone one simply scrolls); blocks taller than the screen stay partly hidden while stacked; cards get the page background behind them (`--sv-page-bg`), their own background paints over it.
- Sections with their own scroll motion (servd scroll-expansion hero, Simmer fridge hero, Stackd stickers) keep it; adding a preset on top can fight it.

---

## 3. Storefront renderer changes (S)

### 3.1 `RenderContext` (PageRenderer.tsx)
Add `editor?: boolean` — set only by the editor frame. When true, `renderSlots` wraps every rendered block in the selection marker.

### 3.2 `PageRenderer.renderSlots` / `BlockSlot`
Today's output for a block is unchanged and is called `inner` below. New wrapping order (outermost first):

`[editor marker]` → `[motion wrapper]` → `inner` (= today's `<>children</>` | `Animate` | `<section>` | `Animate(<section>)`).

```tsx
// per visible block b (after the existing hidden/nested-columns filter):
let out = inner
const m = normalizeMotion(b.motion)
if (m) out = <MotionWrap motion={m} stackIndex={stackIndexOf(b)}>{out}</MotionWrap>
if (ctx?.editor) out = <div data-sv-block={b.id} data-sv-type={b.type} style={{ display: 'contents' }}>{out}</div>
```
- Sticky-stack grouping: after building the list, every maximal run of consecutive visible siblings whose normalised preset is `sticky-stack` is wrapped in `<div className="sv-stack" key={`stack-${firstId}`} style={pageBg}>`; `stackIndexOf` = index within the run. `pageBg` = `{'--sv-page-bg': brandSurface(ctx.section.concept.slug).bg}` when `ctx?.section?.concept` exists, else no style (root default = servd bone). Grouping applies inside columns too (renderSlots(nested=true)).
- A block without valid motion, outside the editor, renders byte-identical markup to today. Keys stay `b.id`.

### 3.3 Selection markers and DOM contract (S emits; the admin never reads the frame DOM)

| marker | element | emitted when | meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `data-sv-block="<id>"` + `data-sv-type="<type>"`, `style="display:contents"` | div around a block's whole output | frame only, for blocks of the EDITED layout incl. column children and pop-up blocks | selection target; `closest('[data-sv-block]')` gives the innermost (a column child before its columns parent) |
| `data-sv-context="<slug>"` | `display:contents` div (servd header: the sticky wrapper itself) around chrome/page parts that are NOT being edited | frame only | click → `context` message (admin offers that part's editor) |
| `.sv-motion[data-sv-motion][data-sv-intensity]`, `.sv-motion-target`, `.sv-motion-pin`, `.sv-motion-track`, `.sv-stack`, `.sv-stack-card[data-sv-stack-first]` | §2.2 | live + frame when motion is valid | scroll effect |
| `data-sv-motion-ready` / `data-sv-m-scrub` | `.sv-motion` | engine / frame preview | §2.5 |
| `#sv-editor-root`, `#sv-editor-overlay` | frame client | frame only | rendered page / outline layer |

Sections: a `section` block's marker wraps whatever its renderer returns; section internals are not separately selectable in this stage (fields are edited in the inspector).

Rect of a marker (frame, viewport CSS px): first element child `E`; if `E` is `.sv-motion` → rect of `E > .sv-motion-pin` if present, else of `E > .sv-motion-target` if present, else of `E` (stack card); otherwise the union of the `getBoundingClientRect()` of the marker's element children with non-zero size, descending through nested `display:contents` children. No visible child → rect `null`.

### 3.4 Other renderer files
- `SiteLayoutView.tsx`: render `<MotionRuntime />` when `hasMotion(blocks)` for the resolved variant. Unchanged otherwise (previewVariant still skips `TrackedLayout`).
- `sections/ManagedPage.tsx`: new prop `editor?: boolean`. It adds `editor: true` to the context ONLY on the `SiteLayoutView` branch (given/live layout with blocks); the "page default sections" branch never gets markers (their ids are not the editor's).
- `components/popups/PopupBlocks.tsx`: new prop `editor?: boolean` → `data-sv-block`/`data-sv-type` on each block's existing wrapper div (recursively into columns). Motion is ignored here.
- `components/popups/PopupHost.tsx`: export `PopupFrame` (existing component) with a new optional prop `editor?: boolean` passed to `PopupBlocks`; the frame uses `track={false}` and a no-op `onClose`. `PopupHost` itself: on the editor-frame path return null and skip the live pop-ups fetch (keep hook order stable: conditions inside effects); add `'editor-frame'` to `RESERVED`.
- Chrome gates stand down on the frame path: `components/StorefrontNav.tsx`, `components/StorefrontFooter.tsx`, `components/feedback/FeedbackSlot.tsx`, `PopupHost` → `if (isEditorFramePath(pathname)) return null`. `isEditorFramePath` lives in a new plain module `src/lib/editorFrame.ts` (no `'use client'`) so the middleware can import it too.
- `sections/pageSurface.tsx` (new): `PageSurface({ slug, children })` — the one definition of each servd page's outer wrapper: `servd:home` → `<div className="sv-home">`; `servd:press`, `servd:location` → `<div style={{ background: 'var(--servd-bg)', color: 'var(--servd-ink)', minHeight: '100dvh' }}>`; `servd:reserve` → same div plus `className="surface-bg"`; anything else → fragment. Switch `app/home/page.tsx`, `app/press/page.tsx`, `app/reserve/page.tsx`, `app/locations/[loc]/page.tsx` to it with byte-identical output (same children, same order). The frame uses the same helper, so frame and live cannot drift.
- SHOULD (hardening, pre-existing risk): in `CtaButton.tsx`, `Hero.tsx` (2 links), `Banner.tsx`, neutralise ONLY script-capable hrefs (`javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:` after trimming, lowercasing and removing whitespace/control chars) to `'#'`; every other href renders exactly as today.
- Docs: `components/blocks/README.md` (Motion.tsx, MotionRuntime, motionClient, motion.css), `sections/README.md` (sections need no change for motion/editor; never rely on being a direct child of `<main>`; no page-level `overflow: hidden`), `src/editor/README.md` (route, protocol, security). Fix the stale "apps/web" comment at the top of `lib/blocks.ts`.

---

## 4. The editor frame route (S)

### 4.1 Files
- `src/app/editor-frame/page.tsx` (server): `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`; `metadata = { title: { absolute: 'Editor preview' }, robots: { index: false, follow: false, nocache: true, googleBot: { index: false, follow: false } }, alternates: { canonical: null } }`; renders `<EditorFrameClient render={renderEditorFrame} allowedOrigins={adminOrigins()} />`. Importing the action here keeps every section/CSS module in this route's graph.
- `src/app/editor-frame/actions.ts` (`'use server'`; exports ONLY async functions): `renderEditorFrame(input: unknown): Promise<FrameRenderResult>`.
- `src/editor/FrameDocument.tsx` (server): composes the page in its real context (§4.3).
- `src/editor/EditorFrameClient.tsx` (`'use client'`): messaging, render scheduling, overlay, input capture, preview.
- `src/editor/protocol.ts`: the shared protocol file (§6), identical to the admin copy.
- `src/editor/types.ts`: S-internal `FrameRenderInput` / `FrameRenderResult`.
- `src/editor/sanitize.ts`: input validation; `src/editor/limits.ts` (or inside actions): rate limit + 30 s caches.

### 4.2 Server action contract (S-internal)
```ts
interface FrameRenderInput {
  rev: number
  slug: string                       // the edited slug, or the context slug for a pop-up backdrop
  edited: null | { title: string | null; blocks: unknown[]; settings: Record<string, unknown> | null; fonts: Array<{ family: string; url: string }> }
  variant: 'a' | 'b'
}
type FrameRenderResult =
  | { ok: true; rev: number; node: React.ReactNode }
  | { ok: false; rev: number; code: 'BAD_INPUT' | 'TOO_LARGE' | 'RATE_LIMITED' | 'RENDER'; error: string }
```
- Validation (`sanitize.ts`): `JSON.stringify(input).length ≤ 600_000` else TOO_LARGE. `slug` parsed with a copy of the backend grammar (`servd:<p>`, `page:<p>`, `brand:<b>[:<p>]`, `popup:<k>`; `PART = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,79}$/i`); the layout kind is DERIVED from the slug (never trusted from input). `variant` ∈ {a,b}. `edited.blocks`: array ≤ 80; each a plain object with string `id` (1–100) and string `type` (≤ 40); `columns` → ≤ 4 arrays of ≤ 40 plain-object blocks, nested `columns` dropped; non-objects dropped. `settings`: plain object or null; keep only `fonts` (strings ≤ 120), `ab` (`splitPct` number, `blocks` sanitised like blocks), `popup` (for pop-ups). `fonts` ≤ 30 entries, family ≤ 120, url ≤ 2000. `title` ≤ 120 or null. The sanitised draft becomes a `SiteLayoutRead` `{ slug, kind, title, version: 0, blocks, settings, fonts, publishedAt: null, updatedAt: null }`. All rendering still goes through the normal renderers (`safe.ts`, `fontFaceCss`, `cssFontFamily`, `normalizeMotion`).
- Rate limit: in-memory per client IP (`cf-connecting-ip`, else first `x-forwarded-for` hop, else `'local'`), 600 renders / minute → RATE_LIMITED (the client retries after 2 s).
- Caches (editor module only, never used by live routes): live layouts of NON-edited parts (`fetchSiteLayout(slug)`) and the concept list (`fetchLiveConcepts()`) cached 30 s in module memory; pass them into `ManagedPage` via its existing `layout` / `concepts` props. Section data (menus, reviews…) is fetched per render as on the live page.
- Wrap the composition in try/catch → `{ ok:false, code:'RENDER', error }`. Errors thrown while the returned tree streams surface client-side (§4.4 error boundary).
- Never read drafts, cookies or staff auth; never write anything.

### 4.3 What the frame renders (FrameDocument)

DRAFT part = `ManagedPage({ slug, layout: draft, previewVariant: variant, editor: true, concepts, ...(params) })`. LIVE part = `ManagedPage({ slug: part, layout: cachedLive(part), previewVariant: 'a', concepts })` wrapped in a `data-sv-context` marker. `previewVariant` on every part means no `TrackedLayout` anywhere → no SiteLayoutStat views/conversions.

| edited slug (kind) | top → bottom |
|---|---|
| `servd:home` / `servd:waitlist` / `servd:press` / `servd:reserve` / `servd:location` / other `servd:<p>` (page) | servd header (live) in `<div data-sv-context="servd:header" style={{position:'sticky',top:0,zIndex:50}}>` → `PageSurface(slug){ DRAFT }` → footer (live, ctx) |
| `page:<x>` (page) | servd header (live) → DRAFT via `SiteLayoutView({ layout: draft, context: { editor: true }, previewVariant })` (mirrors `app/pages/[slug]`, no section context); empty blocks → editor-only note "This page has no elements yet." → footer (live) |
| `servd:header` | DRAFT header inside the same sticky wrapper (no ctx attr) → `PageSurface('servd:home'){ live home }` (ctx `servd:home`) → footer (live) |
| `servd:footer` | header (live) → home (live, ctx) → DRAFT footer |
| `servd:feedback` (widget) | header, home, footer (all live, ctx) → DRAFT feedback widget |
| `brand:<b>`, `brand:<b>:about|visit|menu|<custom>` (page) | `BrandShell(concept themed with brandAccent){ header: live brand:<b>:header (ctx), children: DRAFT, footer: live brand:<b>:footer (ctx) }` |
| `brand:<b>:header` / `:footer` | same shell with the DRAFT in that slot and the live brand home (ctx `brand:<b>`) as the page |
| `popup:<k>` | not rendered by the action; see §4.4 |
| unknown brand | editor-only notice "This brand is not on the storefront." |

- `servd:location`: pass `params: { loc }` = the first location from `fetchBrandLocations` (sorted by name) to the DRAFT part.
- The concept for a brand page: `findConcept(slug, cachedConcepts)` (live row else bundled fallback), themed as in `app/brand/[slug]/layout.tsx`.
- The root layout's own chrome (servd nav, footer, feedback, pop-ups) is suppressed by the gates (§3.4); the frame's own chrome sits inside `<main>` — CSS does not depend on that.
- No JSON-LD, `ConceptViewTracker`, `VisitBeacon`, `HomeSearchParam`, `SearchSheet` in the frame.

### 4.4 Frame client behaviour (`EditorFrameClient`)
1. **Not framed** (`window.parent === window`): show "This page shows a live preview inside Admin → Storefront. Open the page there." and do nothing else.
2. **Listen** to `message` (rules §6.2). **Announce** `ready` (session null) on mount and every 1000 ms until `init` arrives (max 15 times): target = `new URL(document.referrer).origin` when it is in `allowedOrigins`, otherwise post once to EACH allowed origin (non-matching targets are dropped by the browser). Never `'*'`.
3. **Docs**: on `init`/`doc`, reject if `JSON.stringify(doc).length > MAX_DOC_CHARS` (post `error TOO_LARGE`) or malformed (`error BAD_DOC`); else keep `latest = doc` and pump: single flight, latest wins. Page kinds: `await render({ rev, slug, edited: { title, blocks, settings, fonts }, variant })`. Pop-ups: compute `contextSlug` (`settings.popup.brands` has exactly one valid slug → `brand:<that>`, else `servd:home`); call the action with `{ slug: contextSlug, edited: null, variant: 'a' }` only when `contextSlug` changes; render the pop-up client-side with `PopupFrame({ popup: { slug, version: 0, title, blocks: variant b && settings.ab ? settings.ab.blocks : blocks, rules: settings.popup ?? preview rules, fonts }, onClose: noop, track: false, editor: true })`; display `bar` sits in flow ABOVE the backdrop page, `modal`/`corner` are fixed as live.
4. **Commit**: apply results with `startTransition(() => setNode(result))` inside `<Suspense fallback={lastGood}>` and an error boundary keyed by rev whose fallback shows `lastGood` plus a slim banner. After commit (effect), collect `ids` = every `#sv-editor-root [data-sv-block]` id (and the pop-up layer's), redraw outlines, re-apply the preview, run a pending `scroll`, then post `rendered { rev, ok, error, ids, ms }`. Error text: BAD_INPUT "The editor sent something the page can't read." · TOO_LARGE "This page is too large to preview." · RATE_LIMITED "Too many updates at once; catching up." (auto-retry 2 s) · RENDER "Part of the page couldn't be drawn." + message. Before the first result show the servd loader and "Loading the page…".
5. **Input capture** (all `capture: true` on `window`, so page handlers never run): `click`/`auxclick` → `preventDefault()`+`stopPropagation()`; innermost `[data-sv-block]` → select it (outline + post `select`); else `[data-sv-context]` → post `context`; else select null. `submit` → prevent. `keydown`: `Escape` → select the parent marker (or null) and post `select`; `Enter`/`Space` whose target is inside `a, button, [role=button], summary` → prevent (typing into inputs is allowed). `mousemove` (rAF) → hover id; post `hover` only when it changes; `mouseleave` of the document → hover null. The page itself scrolls normally (wheel, touch, keys). The frame never navigates.
6. **Overlay** (`#sv-editor-overlay`: `position:fixed; inset:0; pointer-events:none; z-index:2147483000`): selected = 2 px solid `var(--servd-green)` + `0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--servd-ink) 55%, transparent)` and a label chip (`labels[id] ?? type`, `var(--servd-green)` fill, `var(--servd-on-green)` text, 11 px `var(--font-inter)`); hover = 1 px dashed `var(--servd-purple)` with a `color-mix(… var(--servd-bg) 70% …)` halo; context hover = dotted `var(--servd-mute)` with chip "Live top bar / footer / page — click to edit it". Redraw on scroll/resize (rAF), ResizeObserver on the measured elements, and after each commit. Labels render as text, never HTML.
7. **Preview** (`motion-preview`): store `{id, progress}`; re-apply after every commit. Find `[data-sv-block="id"] > .sv-motion`. Missing → post `motion-preview-ended { reason: 'not-found' }`. On first apply, if the wrapper is off-screen, `scrollIntoView({ block: 'center', behavior: 'instant' })`. Spec `scrub === 'in-place'` → `setScrubProgress(wrapper, p)`; `'scroll'` (sticky-stack) → `scrollStackTo(wrapper, p)`. `progress: null` → `clearScrub` (in-place) / nothing (scroll). A user `wheel`/`touchmove`/scroll key while an in-place preview is active → `clearScrub` + post `motion-preview-ended { reason: 'scrolled' }`.
8. **Admin `select` with `scroll: true`**: scroll the element into view (`block: 'center'`; `behavior: 'smooth'`, or `'auto'` under reduced motion) when less than half of it is visible; if the id is not in the DOM yet, keep it pending until the next commit.

